HBV model implementations

* HBV/HBV_KM.py credits the HBV code written by Kevin McGuire, the R
  translation by J. P. Gannon, and contributions from Jan Seibert's HBV Light.
  Guoqiang Tang translated the R implementation to Python. The referenced
  upstream repository does not declare a license. Confirm redistribution
  terms for the translation before including it in an open-source release.
  https://github.com/VT-Hydroinformatics/16-Intro-Modeling-HBV/blob/master/HBV/HBV.R

* HBV/HBV.py and HBV/HBV_raw.py credit the hydroDL2 HBV implementation. The
  hydroDL2 repository carried Apache-2.0 when the GitHub snapshot was first
  committed in January 2025. Upstream changed its terms in June 2025. The
  exact source revision for the local adaptations is unrecorded. Confirm
  it and retain the applicable upstream license text and notices before
  distributing these adaptations as part of a release.
  https://github.com/mhpi/hydrodl2/blob/65317f672d4497aa4c1bb6ab83bb802e95947f07/LICENSE
  https://github.com/mhpi/hydrodl2/commit/b8b3155c333368d7e663ec510c45fae52d16d02d

Optimization and regionalization dependencies

* The GitHub workflows import MO-ASMO support modules externally. The
  public MO-ASMO repository carries GPL-3.0. The Zenodo snapshot includes
  research copies of some optimization modules and separately attributes
  its RavenPy-derived helper. RavenPy carries the MIT license.
  https://github.com/gongw03/MO-ASMO
  https://github.com/CSHS-CWRA/RavenPy

